INT. BOWLING ALLEY - NIGHT

Neon pins. A banner: LEAGUE FINALS - SPARE ME LANES. Most of the crowd has gone home. Lane 12 is lit.

COACH DELPHINE MARCHAND, 50s, silver bob, orange cardigan, sits with a clipboard on her knee.

GRETA LINDQVIST, 30s, anchor bowler, towels her hands. Her shoulders are rounded in defeat.

RUBEN ACOSTA, 20s, rookie, sits on the ball return with his shoes untied.

DELPHINE
Tenth frame. You left the seven-ten.

GRETA
I know what I left.

RUBEN
It was a hard split.

DELPHINE
It was the hardest split.

GRETA
I shouldn't have gone for it.

DELPHINE
You went for it because it was there.

RUBEN
She was winning on pins, Coach.

GRETA
Don't defend me.

DELPHINE
Ruben, let her talk.

RUBEN
I'm just saying.

GRETA
Eleven years I've been bowling with this team. Eleven.

DELPHINE
Twelve.

GRETA
Twelve. And in twelve years we've never won the final. Not once. And I stood up there tonight and I thought, this is it, this is the one.

RUBEN
You were incredible in the eighth.

GRETA
I was incredible in the eighth. I was terrible in the tenth. That's the whole story.

DELPHINE
It isn't the whole story.

GRETA
It's the only part they'll remember.

DELPHINE
Greta.

GRETA
Delphine, please. I need to say this without you being kind to me.

DELPHINE
All right.

GRETA
I'm thirty-four. My wrist hurts when it rains. My daughter wants me to quit and take her to the lake.

RUBEN
Don't quit.

GRETA
Ruben, you've been here six months.

RUBEN
Don't quit.

DELPHINE
He's right. Stay.

GRETA
You want me to stay because you have no one else.

DELPHINE
I want you to stay because you are the best bowler I've ever coached, and I've coached some very good ones.

RUBEN
She really is.

GRETA
Neither of you is helping.

DELPHINE
We aren't trying to help. We're trying to tell you the truth.

RUBEN
What's the truth?

DELPHINE
The truth is that nobody wins the seven-ten.

GRETA
Somebody has to.

DELPHINE
Somebody has, twice, in the history of the sport. And both of them cried afterward.

RUBEN
Why?

DELPHINE
Because it doesn't feel like winning. It feels like surviving.

GRETA
Is that what this is? Surviving?

DELPHINE
Twelve years, Greta. You're still standing.

RUBEN
I'll buy the nachos.

GRETA
You don't have to buy the nachos.

RUBEN
I'm buying the nachos.

DELPHINE
Get extra cheese.

GRETA
And jalapenos.

RUBEN
That I can do.

DELPHINE
And next season?

GRETA
Next season we try again.

DELPHINE
That's all I wanted to hear.

GRETA
Don't gloat.

DELPHINE
I'm not gloating. I'm planning.

RUBEN
Planning what?

DELPHINE
Everything. Starting with how to teach a rookie to tie his shoes.

RUBEN
I know how to tie my shoes!

GRETA
Then do it.

He looks down. The laces are knotted together. He groans. They laugh. First time all night.
